/T (An LLM is a prediction engine, not a thinking machine. It has read an enormous amount of human text and learned to predict what a useful response looks like  given what you gave it. It has no memory between sessions. It cannot verify facts. It has no agenda. It is extraordinarily good at one thing: producing structured, relevant output when given clear structure and rich context.)
/E (An LLM is a prediction engine, not a thinking machine. It has read an enormous amount of human text and learned to predict what a useful response looks like  given what you gave it. It has no memory between sessions. It cannot verify facts. It has no agenda. It is extraordinarily good at one thing: producing structured, relevant output when given clear structure and rich context.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [8]
