/E (HOW TO USE IT)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
5658 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1723 0 R
/E (AI has no memory of who you are. Every prompt starts from zero. The Context Stack is a four-layer background brief: Situation \(current state\), Background \(relevant history and details\), Constraints \(what limits apply\), Output Format \(exactly how you want the answer\).)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
5659 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1723 0 R
/E (The more precise your stack, the more precise the output.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
5660 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1723 0 R
/E (Constraints is the layer people forget most, which is why AI often suggests things you already know won't work. Background doesn't need to be exhaustive, just the two or three facts that would change the answer if left out. A reused context stack compounds in value across a session, since each new prompt inherits the setup instead of re-explaining it)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
5661 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 12083 0 R
/E (Write your context stack before your actual question, treat it as setup. )
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [11]
>>
