5789 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1727 0 R
/E (HOW TO USE IT)
/Pg 39 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
5790 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1727 0 R
/E (One prompt almost never produces the best result. The Refinement Loop is a four-stage iteration: Draft \(generate first version\), Critique \(ask AI what's weak\), Improve \(ask AI to fix those weaknesses\), Lock \(confirm the final version meets your goal\). Each loop takes under 60 seconds.)
/Pg 39 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
5791 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1727 0 R
/E (Most people stop at Draft. They get an output that is 70% right and move on  leaving the best version unbuilt. The Critique step is the most underused: AI is surprisingly honest when asked to evaluate its own work, surfacing gaps you might not notice yourself. Two loops is almost always enough)
/Pg 39 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
