5917 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1731 0 R
/E (First principles means decomposing a problem to its fundamental truths, stripping away assumptions, analogies, and 'how it's always done', then rebuilding from scratch. Aristotle formalised it. Physicists rely on it. Founders use it to build things that shouldn't be possible by conventional thinking. Most people reason by analogy instead, copying what already exists with small variations, which is faster but caps you at incremental improvements on someone else's idea.)
/Pg 43 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
