/E (Elon Musk used First Principles to reduce SpaceX's rocket cost by 10x. The industry assumption was that rockets cost $65M. He asked: what do the raw materials actually cost? Carbon fibre, aluminium, titanium, copper  about $2M. SpaceX built its own rockets for $6M. The assumption was the business model,  not the physics.)
/Pg 43 0 R
/K [17]
>>
