<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1733 0 R
/E (First-order thinking asks: what happens if I do this? Second-order thinking asks: and then what? And then what after that? Most bad decisions look good at the first level. The consequences that hurt you are almost always second or third order. Howard Marks popularised this in investing. It applies to every business decision.)
/Pg 45 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
