>>
endobj
6048 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1735 0 R
/E (Inversion means solving a problem backwards. Instead of 'how do I succeed?' you ask 'what would guarantee I fail?' Then systematically avoid everything on that list. Charlie Munger called it one of the most useful thinking tools he knew. It surfaces risks that positive thinking consistently misses.)
/Pg 47 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
6049 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1735 0 R
/E (Listing paths to failure is concrete and finite, while listing paths to success is easy to fool yourself with. The founders who last usually wrote the failure list first and took it seriously.)
/Pg 47 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
