6115 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1737 0 R
/E (A mental model is a simplified map of how something works. The best founders carry a library of them. Pareto's 80/20 shows where leverage hides. Parkinson's Law explains why work expands to fill time. Dunning-Kruger maps confidence vs competence. The Iceberg Model shows what's visible vs what's driving behaviour beneath the surface. The value isn't memorizing the list, it's reaching for the right model at the right moment, the way a mechanic reaches for the right tool without thinking about the whole toolbox.)
/Pg 49 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
