/P 1741 0 R
/E (SCAMPER is a structured creativity tool built on seven lenses: Substitute \(what can be replaced?\), Combine \(what can be merged?\), Adapt \(what can be borrowed from elsewhere?\), Modify or Magnify \(what can be changed or amplified?\), Put to other uses \(what else could this do?\), Eliminate \(what can be removed?\), Reverse or Rearrange \(what if we flipped the order?\). Each lens forces a different angle on the same problem. Originally developed by Bob Eberle, building on Alex Osborn's brainstorming work.)
/Pg 53 0 R
/K [9]
>>
