6408 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1746 0 R
/E (Developed by Alexander Osterwalder, the Value Proposition Canvas maps two things side by side: your Customer Profile \(what jobs they're trying to do, what pains they experience, what gains they want\) and your Value Map \(your products and services, pain relievers, gain creators\). Product-market fit happens when your Value Map directly addresses the most important items in the Customer Profile. Most product failures happen because founders built the Value Map first, then looked for customers to match.)
/Pg 58 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
6409 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1746 0 R
/E (The canvas works best as a living document, not a one-time exercise. As you talk to customers, your understanding of their jobs and pains sharpens  and your Value Map should shift to match. A canvas that never changes after the first draft is a sign that no real customer conversation has happened yet.)
/Pg 58 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
