<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1754 0 R
/E (Your customers describe your product differently than you do. Your retention is lower than it should be. People churn and you don't understand why. You're optimising features nobody really cares about.)
/Pg 66 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
6632 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1754 0 R
/E (HOW TO USE IT)
/Pg 66 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
6633 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1754 0 R
/E (Developed by Clayton Christensen at Harvard Business School, Jobs To Be Done \(JTBD\) is a lens for understanding why customers 'hire' a product. People don't buy products,  they hire them to do a job. That job has three layers: a Functional job \(the practical task\), a Social job \(how they want to be seen doing it\), and an Emotional job \(how they want to feel\). The product that best does all three layers of the job wins. Most products only address the functional layer.)
/Pg 66 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
6634 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 12390 0 R
/E (Interview 5 real customers using the JTBD prompt below,  don't survey, talk. )
/Pg 66 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
6635 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 12391 0 R
/E (Focus on the moment they decided to look for a solution, that's where the real job lives.)
/Pg 66 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
