6692 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1756 0 R
/E (The Minimum Viable Product concept, popularised by Eric Ries in The Lean Startup, is about finding the smallest version of your product that delivers enough value to attract early customers and generate real learning. MVP does not mean low quality,  it means maximum learning for minimum investment. The question is not 'what is the smallest thing we can build?' but 'what is the smallest thing that will tell us if we're right?')
/Pg 68 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
