6754 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1758 0 R
/E (The Value Ladder is a pricing architecture where you offer a sequence of increasingly valuable products or services at ascending price points. Each level delivers genuine value and naturally leads the customer to want the next. Russell Brunson popularised this in digital products; it applies equally to B2B services, SaaS, and physical products. The goal is to have an offer at every level of customer readiness and budget  from free entry to high-ticket.)
/Pg 70 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
