/E (Warren Buffett's concept of an economic moat describes a sustainable competitive advantage that protects a business from competition the way a moat protects a castle. The five types of moat are: Network Effects \(the product gets better as more people use it\), Cost Advantage \(you produce at lower cost than anyone\), Switching Costs \(customers are locked in by habit, data, or integrations\), Intangible Assets \(brands, patents, licences\), and Efficient Scale \(a market so small only one player can profitably serve it\). Most businesses have weak or no moats. Building one is a strategic choice.)
/Pg 72 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
