6942 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1764 0 R
/E (Developed by Professor Noriaki Kano at Tokyo University of Science in 1984, the Kano Model classifies product features into three types: Basic Needs \(expected, their absence causes dissatisfaction but their presence goes unnoticed\), Performance Needs \(more is better  these features directly drive satisfaction\), and Excitement Needs \(unexpected,  their presence delights, their absence is not missed\). Features also evolve over time: today's excitement becomes tomorrow's basic need. AI can help you classify your features and decide where to invest.)
/Pg 76 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
