>>
endobj
7437 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1779 0 R
/E (Al Ries and Jack Trout established in their 1981 work Positioning: The Battle for Your Mind that positioning is not what you do to a product,  it is what you do to the mind of a prospect. Most businesses position by accident: they describe what they do and hope the right customer self-selects. Deliberate positioning works the opposite way  you choose the customer, the category, and the comparison point, then build every word of your message to reinforce that choice. The goal is a statement so specific it automatically excludes the wrong customer and makes the right one feel it was written for them.)
/Pg 91 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
7438 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 12640 0 R
/E (Draft three positioning statements before deciding  AI can generate all three. )
/Pg 91 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
7439 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 12641 0 R
/E (Test each one: does it exclude anyone? If it appeals to everyone, it works for no one.)
/Pg 91 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
