/P 1785 0 R
/E (Perceptual mapping is a visual tool used in marketing strategy to plot how customers perceive brands or products relative to each other on key dimensions. The two axes represent the attributes that most influence customer choice in your market,  typically price vs quality, or specialist vs generalist, or traditional vs innovative. Where you land on the map reflects customer perception, not your own. AI can generate a perceptual map description and help you identify where the white spaces and repositioning opportunities are.)
/Pg 97 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
