7733 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1788 0 R
/E (AIDA is one of the oldest marketing frameworks in existence, created by Elias St. Elmo Lewis in 1898. It maps the journey from cold contact to action: Attention \(stop the scroll - make them read the first line\), Interest \(build relevance - make them feel this is about them\), Desire \(create urgency - make them want the outcome\), Action \(clear single next step\). Most cold outreach fails at Attention. The first line of any message must be so relevant or intriguing that not reading the rest feels like a loss.)
/Pg 100 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
7734 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
