7800 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1790 0 R
/E (You're talking too much and pitching too early on discovery calls. You leave without fully understanding what the prospect actually needs  and they leave without feeling heard.)
/Pg 102 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
7801 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1790 0 R
/E (HOW TO USE IT)
/Pg 102 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
7802 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1790 0 R
/E (Neil Rackham analysed 35,000 sales calls over 12 years and found that high-value sales are won through questions, not pitches. SPIN replaces pitching with structured questioning:)
/Pg 102 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
7803 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1790 0 R
/E (Situation questions establish context, Problem questions surface pain, Implication)
/Pg 102 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
7804 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1790 0 R
/E (questions show the cost of inaction, Need-Payoff questions let the prospect articulate why they need your solution in their own words. The prospect who convinces themselves is the easiest to close.)
/Pg 102 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
7805 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1790 0 R
/E (Skipping Implication is what makes a close feel pushed rather than earned. A prospect who says out loud why the problem matters will defend that far harder than any pitch could.)
/Pg 102 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
7806 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 12744 0 R
/E (Prepare 3 questions for each SPIN stage before every call  use the prompt below. )
/Pg 102 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
7807 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 12745 0 R
/E (Ask all Situation questions first, then move to Problem. Never pitch before Need-Payoff)
/Pg 102 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
