7995 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1796 0 R
/E (A prospect raises an objection and you immediately counter it with a feature or a price justification. They feel unheard, push back harder, and the conversation dies. You're winning arguments and losing deals.)
/Pg 108 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
7996 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1796 0 R
/E (HOW TO USE IT)
/Pg 108 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
7997 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1796 0 R
/E (Developed by Carew International, the LAER model is a four-step objection response framework built on one principle: an objection is a request for more information, not an attack to defend against. Listen \(fully, without interrupting\), Acknowledge \(validate their concern before responding\), Explore \(ask a question to understand the objection more deeply\), and Respond \(only now address it  with precision\). Skipping Explore is the most common mistake. Most objections have a deeper concern underneath the surface one.)
/Pg 108 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
7998 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 12814 0 R
/E (Never respond to an objection in the same breath you heard it, pause. )
/Pg 108 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
7999 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 12815 0 R
/E (Acknowledge before you explore - validation opens people, defence closes them. )
/Pg 108 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
8000 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 12816 0 R
/E (Use the Explore question to find what is really underneath the objection. )
/Pg 108 0 R
/K [10]
>>
