8117 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 1800 0 R
/T (A Win Story is a proposal structure that mirrors how humans make decisions -  through narrative, not specifications. The structure has six parts: Situation \(their world as it is today\), Complication \(the problem and its cost\), Resolution \(what success looks like\), Solution \(your approach- positioned as the bridge from complication to resolution\), Proof \(evidence that you can deliver\), and Call to Action \(one clear, specific next step\). The key difference from a standard proposal is that the customer's story comes first. Your solution is a supporting character, not the lead.)
/E (A Win Story is a proposal structure that mirrors how humans make decisions -  through narrative, not specifications. The structure has six parts: Situation \(their world as it is today\), Complication \(the problem and its cost\), Resolution \(what success looks like\), Solution \(your approach- positioned as the bridge from complication to resolution\), Proof \(evidence that you can deliver\), and Call to Action \(one clear, specific next step\). The key difference from a standard proposal is that the customer's story comes first. Your solution is a supporting character, not the lead.)
/Pg 112 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
