>>
endobj
8188 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1802 0 R
/E (You send one follow-up after a meeting or proposal and then give up if you hear nothing. You assume silence means no. But most deals are decided after the fifth or sixth touchpoint and you're stopping at two.)
/Pg 114 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
8189 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1802 0 R
/E (HOW TO USE IT)
/Pg 114 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
8190 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1802 0 R
/E (Research in B2B sales consistently shows that 80% of sales require five or more follow-ups, yet 44% of salespeople give up after one. A follow-up sequence is a multi-touch, multi-channel cadence of value-adding contacts that keeps you visible without being pushy. Each touch should add something new, a relevant insight, a case study, an answer to an unanswered question  rather than asking 'just checking in.' AI can build an entire sequence for a specific deal in minutes.)
/Pg 114 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
8191 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 12871 0 R
/E (Never follow up with 'just checking in'  every touch must add value. )
/Pg 114 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
