8342 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1806 0 R
/E (You reach the end of a great sales conversation and don't know how to move it forward. Or you default to the same closing approach every time and it stops working for certain prospect types.)
/Pg 118 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
8343 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1806 0 R
/E (HOW TO USE IT)
/Pg 118 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
8344 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1806 0 R
/E (Closing is not a single technique  it is a set of contextual tools. Different situations require different approaches. The Summary Close \(recap all agreed value, then ask for the decision\) works when the prospect is convinced but hesitant. The Alternative Close \(offer two options, both of which move forward\) works when they're stuck on one variable. The Assumptive Close \(proceed as if the decision is made, surface any remaining concerns\) works when signals are positive. The Question Close \(ask what would make them comfortable to proceed\) works when the real objection hasn't been named. AI can help you identify which close fits your current deal situation.)
/Pg 118 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
8345 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 12907 0 R
/E (Never try to close before the prospect has confirmed the value and urgency.)
/Pg 118 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
8346 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 12908 0 R
/E ( Match the close to the prospect's personality  analytical buyers hate assumptive closes.)
/Pg 118 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
